From b78a225709097da1191731d59077b87ce940ef67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sri Krishna <93153132+srikrsna-buf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Dec 2025 06:15:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Always provide all available variables (#297)

Closes #296

Because of the partial evaluation step, `rules` and `rule` were
optimized away for standard rules so far. For some reason, cel-go is
unable to do the same for field masks. Since this is not clearly
defined, we should always provide them.

Signed-off-by: Sri Krishna <skrishna@buf.build>

Backport of b90590ade1f6eafc98b9d99075451121a884f7a5:
Apply the runtime rule binding to the v0.12.0 activation chain. Retain
its existing rules globals and variable pool; omit the newer bindings
refactor and field-mask fixtures, which require newer protobuf schemas.
This also preserves repeated predefined rules with cel-go v0.30.0.
---
 program.go | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/program.go b/program.go
index a974876..a115dba 100644
--- a/program.go
+++ b/program.go
@@ -111,6 +111,10 @@ func (expr compiledProgram) eval(bindings *variable, cfg *validationConfig) (*Vi
 	now := globalNowPool.Get(cfg.nowFn)
 	defer globalNowPool.Put(now)
 	bindings.Next = now
+	// Partial evaluation may leave references to the predefined rule value.
+	if expr.Value.IsValid() {
+		bindings.Next = &variable{Name: "rule", Val: expr.Value.Interface(), Next: now}
+	}
 
 	value, _, err := expr.Program.Eval(bindings)
 	if err != nil {
-- 
